# Build context for Dockerfile.app ONLY. BuildKit picks up
# "<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore" in preference to the shared .dockerignore,
# which is what makes this possible.
#
# Why it exists: the shared .dockerignore deliberately does NOT exclude *.gguf,
# because Dockerfile.llm COPYs two of the model files out of the build context
# by exact name. The app image COPYs none of them -- it talks to the LLM
# container over HTTP -- but it was still paying for them: every `docker build
# -f Dockerfile.app` shipped ~28GB of model weights to the daemon before the
# first instruction ran, several minutes of pure transfer for files no layer
# reads. Excluding them here leaves Dockerfile.llm's context untouched.
#
# Keep the rest in step with .dockerignore.

*.gguf

.git
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
backups/
logs/
data/
VAPT/
samples/
documents/
"aa audit evidence samples/"
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
qa/
scratch/
.claude/
.vscode/
*.exe
*.pem
*.tar
*.zip
*.pdf
dist/
build/
temp_clean_repo_export/
.pytest_cache/

# The embedding cache of the documents scanned on the build machine -- file
# names included, some of them client documents. COPY src/ carried it into
# app 1.1. The app starts without it and rebuilds it from the customer's own
# documents. (This file, not .dockerignore, is the one the app build reads.)
src/core/.embeddings_cache.pkl
